From 091eb35dfa61e4669d0c23dfd38efa25c8497999 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TeamHarrisCali <34009957+TeamHarrisCali@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:28:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Wi-Fi window: the DSi chip (wlan0) for open and WPA2 networks

- dsiwifi.c: /proc/dsiwifi2nets (a state line, then the last scan in
  /proc/dswifi's format) and a "scan" command (not while connected).
- dsnet (Start > Network > Wi-Fi): uses the DSi chip when its firmware
  file is installed, unless the DS chip is already on; button
  "DSi chip" / "DS chip" (key c) switches, taking the other one down.
  DSi chip: loads the firmware file once, ifconfig wlan0 up (up to a
  minute), asks for a WPA2 password (8-63 characters), writes psk and
  connect straight to /proc/dsiwifi2 (no shell), waits up to 100 s for
  the connection (and the WPA2 keys), DHCP on wlan0, saves the network
  in /home/wifi.known, its name in /tmp/wifi.current. WEP stays with
  the DS chip, WPA2 with the DSi chip; each says so.
- dsdesk: the tray watches nds and wlan0; the tooltip names the DSi
  chip's network from /tmp/wifi.current.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
